    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2025-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>In this question you must show all stages of your working. Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(z) = 4z^3 - 12z^2 - 95z + 325\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(-5) = 0\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) determine <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(z)\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(z + a)(bz^2 + cz + d)\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a, b, c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are integers.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Hence show that the complex roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(z) = 0\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{8 \\pm i}{2}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(2z - 1) = 0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
