    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2025-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>(i)</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf P = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; 1 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Describe fully the single geometrical transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf P\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) State the equation of one invariant line under the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(ii)</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf Q = \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos 2\\theta &amp; 0 \\\\ 1 &amp; \\tan 2\\theta \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0 \\leq \\theta &lt; 360^\\circ\"></span></p><p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf Q\"></span> represents the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><p>Triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> is transformed to triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T&#x27;\"></span> by the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the coordinates of the vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2, 3), (3, 6)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8, 3)\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T&#x27;\"></span> is 4.5</li></ul><p>determine the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span></p><p>(Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.)</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></p>",
