    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2025-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>A complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> is represented by the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> in the complex plane.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> satisfies</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|z - 1| = 1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) sketch on an Argand diagram the locus of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> varies.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> also satisfies</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\arg(z + 1) = \\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) determine the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> such that the locus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arg(z + 1) = \\theta\"></span> is a tangent to the locus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|z - 1| = 1\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Hence determine the exact possible complex numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
