    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2025-june/q7",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:152mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8fm0-01-2025-june/q07-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figures 1 and 2. Balloon with the 24 m height indicated, and curve C on the coordinate axes.\"></figure><p>In this question you must show all stages of your working. Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of a hot air balloon.</p><p>When filled with air the balloon has a height of 24 metres.</p><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"350x^2 = (12 + y)^2 (A - y^2) \\quad x \\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>The balloon is modelled by rotating <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis.</p><p>Given that one <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> intercept of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-12\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A = 144\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Use algebraic integration to determine the volume of air needed to fill the balloon, according to the model, giving the answer to 2 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Modify the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"350x^2 = (12 + y)^2 (144 - y^2)\"></span> to model a mathematically similar balloon with a height of 26 metres.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) State one limitation of the models.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
