      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2025-june/q8",
      "question": "<p>The first <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> triangular numbers are</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1, 3, 6, 10, \\ldots, \\frac{1}{2}n(n+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> is a positive integer.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the standard results for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r\"></span> to show that the sum of the first <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> triangular numbers is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1}{6}n(n+1)(n+2)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Hence determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> for which the sum of the first <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> triangular numbers is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"22n\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
