    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2025-june/q9",
      "question": "<p>An engineer detects a source of water below the surface of the ground. The engineer models the situation relative to a fixed origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>.</p><p>In the model</p><ul><li>the surface of the ground is a plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x - 2y + 8z = 1\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>the source of water is at a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6, -2, -4)\"></span></li></ul><p>where the units are metres.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the model to determine the shortest distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> to the surface of the ground.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) By considering the model, comment on whether the answer to part (a) is reliable, giving a reason for your answer.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>To access the water, a hole is drilled, in a straight line, from a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> on the surface of the ground to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span>.</p><p>Given that the length of the hole needs to be as short as possible,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) determine the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, according to the model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>Given that the actual length of the hole drilled is 2.52 metres,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) use the answer to part (a) to evaluate the model, giving a reason for your answer.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
